+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope; Free-Text Veterinarian Search Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Whether it was deliberate stayed unknown.
+
+A request on 2026-10-24 asks to narrow the veterinarian directory to the veterinarians holding one named specialty. Read literally, NG-9 declines that. The owner decided the row at intake (2026-10-24):
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the request. Rejected by the owner's decision above.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Open every kind of veterinarian, pet, and visit search. Rejected: the owner kept free-text veterinarian search out of scope, and the decision does not touch pets or visits.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text search stays declined. Narrowing the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 still declines free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. It no longer declines narrowing the veterinarian directory by an attribute the directory already shows. Specialty is the first such attribute requested, under REQ-VET-003.
+
+The narrowing adds no page control. The owner scoped the request to the page address, and deferred a visible control to a possible follow-up request.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation; the Non-Goals preamble names it decided.
+- REQ-VET-003 narrows both forms of the directory by specialty. REQ-VET-004 reinstates the machine-readable form as a supported capability.
+- A request to search veterinarians by free text, or to search pets or visits, still meets NG-9. It proceeds only on an explicit owner decision recorded at intake.
+- A visible control for the narrowing is an open question, not a non-goal.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row and the preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — REQ-VET-003 and REQ-VET-004.
