+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also offered in a machine-readable form, holding every veterinarian with their specialties in one document `[REQ-VET-004]`.
+
+Either form can be narrowed to the veterinarians holding one named specialty, given in the request address `[REQ-VET-003]`. The name matches a specialty's whole name, disregarding letter case; the start of a name alone matches nothing. A blank name leaves the directory unnarrowed, as an empty owner search does. No page control offers the narrowing yet. It is reached by address alone, and moving between pages keeps it in place.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the machine-readable directory is requested without a specialty, then every veterinarian is returned with their specialties.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty, when the directory is opened, then only veterinarians holding it are listed, a page at a time over the narrowed list.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty, when the machine-readable directory is requested, then only veterinarians holding it are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a name differing from a specialty's name only by letter case, when either form is requested, then it narrows to that specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given only the start of a specialty's name, when either form is requested, then no veterinarian is returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a name no veterinarian's specialty matches, when either form is requested, then the normal page or document is returned with an empty list, not an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or all-space name, when either form is requested, then the result equals the request with no name given.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a narrowed directory spanning more than one page, when the reader moves to another page, then the narrowing still applies.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. ~~**Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form, carrying no requirement.~~ **Resolved 2026-10-24:** the owner reinstated the machine-readable form as `[REQ-VET-004]`.
+3. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears once in a narrowed list, still shown with every specialty they hold.
+4. A veterinarian holding no specialty never appears in a narrowed list.
+5. A name that is no specialty at all yields the same empty result as a specialty no veterinarian holds.
 
